IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-ch1-preliminary`

-- Tests for act-ch1-preliminary.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 1, Preliminary`

§§ `ss 2 and 2A: the dictionary is part of this Act; a note is not`

-- s 2: "The dictionary at the end of this Act is part of this Act."
#ASSERT `s 2: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2 says` `the dictionary at the end of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 2 says nothing about a note or any other provision.
#ASSERT `s 2: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2 says` `a note included in this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2 says` `any other provision of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2A: "A note included in this Act is explanatory and is not part of this Act."
#ASSERT `s 2A: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2A says` `a note included in this Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2A says nothing about the dictionary or any other provision.
#ASSERT `s 2A: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2A says` `the dictionary at the end of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2A: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2A says` `any other provision of this Act` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4: what this Act applies to`

-- s 4 (1): "This Act applies to all Acts (including this Act) and statutory instruments."
#ASSERT `s 4 (1): this Act applies to the thing` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 (1): this Act applies to the thing` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The sentence has no "only", so a thing that is neither is not answered.
#ASSERT `s 4 (1): this Act applies to the thing` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4 (2): "Acts and statutory instruments are taken to be made on the basis that they will operate in conjunction with this Act."
#ASSERT `s 4 (2): the thing is taken to be made on the basis that it will operate in conjunction with this Act` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 (2): the thing is taken to be made on the basis that it will operate in conjunction with this Act` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 (2): the thing is taken to be made on the basis that it will operate in conjunction with this Act` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4 (2) Example 1 and Example 2: the XYZ Act 2001 is an Act, so it is taken to be made on that basis.
#ASSERT `s 4 (2): the thing is taken to be made on the basis that it will operate in conjunction with this Act` `an Act (including this Act)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 6: when a provision of this Act is displaced`

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: determinative, expressly displaced` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS TRUE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS TRUE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS FALSE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: determinative, manifest contrary intention` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS TRUE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS TRUE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS TRUE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: determinative, contrary intention that is not manifest` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS TRUE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS TRUE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: non-determinative, contrary intention` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS FALSE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS TRUE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: non-determinative, nothing relied on` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS FALSE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS FALSE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: non-determinative, concurrent operation and the same subject matter` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS FALSE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS FALSE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS TRUE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Facts about a possible displacement`
`facts: non-determinative, same subject matter only` MEANS
    `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
        `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS FALSE
        `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS FALSE
        `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS FALSE
        `the contrary intention is manifest` IS FALSE
        `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
        `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS TRUE

-- s 6 (8) Example 1 (determinative provision, express displacement): "Section 83 (2) illustrates a provision expressly displacing this Act, s 47 (3), a determinative provision."
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: determinative, expressly displaced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 (1): the provision of this Act must be applied to the Act or statutory instrument` `facts: determinative, expressly displaced` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6 (8) Example 2 (determinative provision, manifest contrary intention): s 79 (3) displaces s 47 (3) "by a manifest contrary intention".
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: determinative, manifest contrary intention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6 (2): a determinative provision may be displaced expressly or by a manifest contrary intention; a contrary intention that is not manifest is not one of the two, and the text does not say it fails.
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: determinative, contrary intention that is not manifest` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6 (8) Example 3 (non-determinative provision, contrary intention): "the reference to 'master' indicates a contrary intention".
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: non-determinative, contrary intention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6 (3): with no express displacement and no contrary intention, the text does not say the provision is displaced or is not.
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: non-determinative, nothing relied on` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 (1): the provision of this Act must be applied to the Act or statutory instrument` `facts: non-determinative, nothing relied on` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6 (8) Example (concurrent operation): s 247 is not displaced by the Small Clubs Act 2002, s 60, because the two "can operate concurrently" (s 6 (6)) and deal with the same subject matter (s 6 (7)).
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: non-determinative, concurrent operation and the same subject matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6 (1): the provision of this Act must be applied to the Act or statutory instrument` `facts: non-determinative, concurrent operation and the same subject matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6 (7): a provision is not displaced because the provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter.
#ASSERT `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `facts: non-determinative, same subject matter only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6 (4): a more deliberate displacement is required for a determinative provision.
#ASSERT `s 6 (4): how deliberate a displacement of the provision must be` TRUE EQUALS `a more deliberate displacement`
#ASSERT `s 6 (4): how deliberate a displacement of the provision must be` FALSE EQUALS `a displacement that is not more deliberate than usual`
-- s 6 (5): "This section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation."
#ASSERT `s 6 (5): this section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 (5): this section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation` FALSE

§§ `Part 1.2: what an Act, a subordinate law and the other kinds of document are`

GIVEN alsoByLaw IS A BOOLEAN, madeUnder IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a document made under` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS TRUE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS madeUnder
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS alsoByLaw
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

GIVEN declaredBy IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS declaredBy
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

GIVEN declaredBy IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS declaredBy
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

GIVEN commencementOf IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS commencementOf

GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a fee determination by a Minister under an Act` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS TRUE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a law of the Legislative Assembly` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS TRUE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS TRUE
        `is made under` IS EMPTY
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
`a thing that is not a document` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment or instrument` WITH
        `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS FALSE
        `is a regulation or rule` IS FALSE
        `is any writing or other document` IS FALSE
        `is made under` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS LIST `an Act`
        `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS FALSE
        `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS EMPTY
        `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS EMPTY

-- s 7 (1), (2): an Act is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act.
#ASSERT `s 7 (1), (2): the document is an Act` `a law of the Legislative Assembly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 (1), (2): the document is an Act` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8 (1): a subordinate law is a regulation or rule made under (a) an Act, (b) another subordinate law, or (c) power given by an Act or subordinate law and also power given otherwise by law.
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `a subordinate law`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a document made under` TRUE (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Made under a disallowable instrument only: none of (a), (b) or (c).
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `a disallowable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made under power given otherwise by law only: none of (a), (b) or (c).
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a document made under` TRUE EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a regulation or rule.
#ASSERT `s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` (`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 9 (1) (a): a statutory instrument declared to be a disallowable instrument by an Act, subordinate law or another disallowable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` (LIST `a subordinate law`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` (LIST `a disallowable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Declared by a commencement notice: not one of the three declarers named.
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared disallowable by` (LIST `a commencement notice`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9 (1) (b): a determination of fees or charges by a Minister under an Act or subordinate law.
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` `a fee determination by a Minister under an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Declared by an Act, but not a statutory instrument (not a document at all): limb (a) needs a statutory instrument.
#ASSERT `s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` `a thing that is not a document` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 10 (1): a statutory instrument declared a notifiable instrument by an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or another notifiable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` (LIST `a subordinate law`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` (LIST `a disallowable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` (LIST `a notifiable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` (LIST `a commencement notice`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` (`a statutory instrument declared notifiable by` EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 11 (1): a statutory instrument that fixes or otherwise determines the commencement of an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or notifiable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` (LIST `a subordinate law`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` (LIST `a disallowable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` (LIST `a notifiable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Fixes the commencement of a commencement notice: not one of the four kinds named.
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` (LIST `a commencement notice`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` (`a statutory instrument fixing the commencement of` EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 12 (1): a legislative instrument is a subordinate law, disallowable instrument, notifiable instrument or commencement notice.
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `a subordinate law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `a disallowable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `a notifiable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `a commencement notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `an Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` `a statutory instrument of another kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 13 (1): a statutory instrument is an instrument made under (a) an Act, (b) another statutory instrument, or (c) power given by an Act or statutory instrument and also power given otherwise by law.
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `a notifiable instrument`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `a statutory instrument of another kind`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` (`a document made under` TRUE (LIST `a commencement notice`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Made under power given otherwise by law only: none of (a), (b) or (c).
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` (`a document made under` TRUE EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` `a thing that is not a document` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 13 (2): "A statutory instrument includes a subordinate law, disallowable instrument, notifiable instrument and commencement notice."
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `a subordinate law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `a disallowable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `a notifiable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `a commencement notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "includes" does not close the list.
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` `a statutory instrument of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 14 (1): an instrument is any writing or other document.
#ASSERT `s 14 (1): the document is an instrument` (`a document made under` FALSE (LIST `an Act`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 (1): the document is an instrument` `a thing that is not a document` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 15 (1): a republication of a law authorised by the parliamentary counsel under this Act.
#ASSERT `s 15 (1): the republication is an authorised republication` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15 (1): the republication is an authorised republication` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15 (1): the republication is an authorised republication` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 7 (3), s 8 (2), s 9 (2), s 10 (2), s 11 (2), s 12 (2), s 13 (3), s 14 (2), s 15 (2): "A reference to an X includes a reference to a provision of an X."
#ASSERT `s 7 (3): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 (3): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a provision of it` `a subordinate law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8 (2): a reference to a subordinate law includes a reference to a provision of it` `a subordinate law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8 (2): a reference to a subordinate law includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9 (2): a reference to a disallowable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `a disallowable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9 (2): a reference to a disallowable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10 (2): a reference to a notifiable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `a notifiable instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 (2): a reference to a notifiable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11 (2): a reference to a commencement notice includes a reference to a provision of it` `a commencement notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 (2): a reference to a commencement notice includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12 (2): a reference to a legislative instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `a legislative instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12 (2): a reference to a legislative instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13 (3): a reference to a statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `a statutory instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13 (3): a reference to a statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14 (2): a reference to an instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `an instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 (2): a reference to an instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15 (2): a reference to an authorised republication includes a reference to a provision of it` `an authorised republication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15 (2): a reference to an authorised republication includes a reference to a provision of it` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 16: a provision is any words or anything else that forms part of the Act or instrument.
#ASSERT `s 16: the words or other thing are a provision of the Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16: the words or other thing are a provision of the Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16 Examples—provisions consisting of groups of words: sections, subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs, sub-subparagraphs, examples.
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a section` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a subsection` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a paragraph` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a subparagraph` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a sub-subparagraph` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `an example` EQUALS JUST `a group of words`
-- s 16 Examples—provisions consisting of groups of other provisions: chapters, parts, divisions, subdivisions, schedules.
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a chapter` EQUALS JUST `a group of other provisions`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a part` EQUALS JUST `a group of other provisions`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a division` EQUALS JUST `a group of other provisions`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a subdivision` EQUALS JUST `a group of other provisions`
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `a schedule` EQUALS JUST `a group of other provisions`
-- The examples are not an exhaustive list.
#ASSERT `s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 17: references to Acts include former enactments`

#ASSERT `s 17 (1), (2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to the enactment` `an Act of the Legislative Assembly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 (1), (2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to the enactment` `a former Commonwealth enactment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 (1), (2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to the enactment` `a former NSW Act or former UK Act mentioned in schedule 1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 (1), (2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to the enactment` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

GIVEN isCwlthOrNswOrImperial IS A BOOLEAN, sg34 IS A BOOLEAN, cp1012 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a former enactment`
`a candidate enactment` MEANS
    `Facts about a former enactment` WITH
        `is a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or an Imperial Act` IS isCwlthOrNswOrImperial
        `is an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34` IS sg34
        `is an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3)` IS cp1012

-- s 17 (3) (a): an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34.
#ASSERT `s 17 (3): the enactment is a former Commonwealth enactment` (`a candidate enactment` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 17 (3) (b): an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3).
#ASSERT `s 17 (3): the enactment is a former Commonwealth enactment` (`a candidate enactment` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A Commonwealth Act, NSW Act or Imperial Act that is neither (a) nor (b).
#ASSERT `s 17 (3): the enactment is a former Commonwealth enactment` (`a candidate enactment` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or an Imperial Act.
#ASSERT `s 17 (3): the enactment is a former Commonwealth enactment` (`a candidate enactment` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
